<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market no help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market no help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it did not invite operations at 1330 GMT after revising its money market shortage forecast to 1.5 billion stg.</p>
<p>Earlier in the session, the Bank allotted a total of 1.5 billion stg in assistance to the money market, leaving no residual shortage.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
